<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33005" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ōrīthȳīa</span></b> 
			(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quadrisyl.</span></b> ),
			ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὠρείθυια</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>a female proper name.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Erechtheus</i>, <i>king
				of Athens; who became by Boreas the mother of Calaïs
				and Zetes</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6, 683</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 4,
				463</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. A. 12, 83</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8, 5,
				16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Leg. 1, 1,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A queen of the Amazons</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 2, 4,
				17</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
